From 7157000000000000000000000000000000000008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RistOS Build <build@ristos.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] rist: do not lock a task that was removed while its lock
 transition was queued

An activity whose task is lock-task launchable (android:lockTaskMode, or an
allowlisted task while the device is already locked) makes
realStartActivityLocked queue a TRANSIT_START_LOCK_TASK_MODE transition with
startCollectOrQueue. If another transition is still collecting (typical on a
sleeping, keyguard-locked phone), the lambda runs later. If the process is
killed or force-stopped in the meantime, the task is removed from the
hierarchy. A detached Task is its own root task and has no display area, so
the lambda's startLockTaskMode -> setLockTaskMode -> findTaskToMoveToFront
passes the null-root check and dereferences a null TaskDisplayArea in
moveHomeRootTaskToFrontIfNeeded. That is an uncaught NPE on android.display:
system_server dies and the phone soft-reboots.

Observed on rist.2026090701 (twice): an instrumentation run force-stopped the
home/kiosk app twice within one pending OPEN transition; the lambda queued for
the first, already removed, task ran when the queue drained.

ActivityTaskManagerService.startSystemLockTaskMode already guards its own
queued lambda with `deferred && !task.isAttached()`; this adds the same guard
to realStartActivityLocked, and a backstop in LockTaskController so no caller
can lock a detached task.

Apply from the frameworks/base git project with `git am`; independent of the
other patches. Context is from the GrapheneOS `17` branch, whose line numbers
match the crash stack exactly (ActivityTaskSupervisor.java:916/1691/1725,
LockTaskController.java:688/766), and may drift on another sync (use
`patch -p1 --fuzz=3`, or regenerate with `git format-patch`).
---
 services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityTaskSupervisor.java | 12 ++++++++++++
 services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/LockTaskController.java     |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityTaskSupervisor.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityTaskSupervisor.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityTaskSupervisor.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityTaskSupervisor.java
@@ -905,5 +905,17 @@
                     task.mTransitionController.startCollectOrQueue(transition,
                             (deferred) -> {
+                                // RistOS: the queued lambda can run after the task was removed
+                                // (process killed or force-stopped while an earlier transition
+                                // was still collecting). A removed Task is its own root and has
+                                // no display area, so startLockTaskMode would NPE in
+                                // moveHomeRootTaskToFrontIfNeeded and take down system_server.
+                                // Same guard as startSystemLockTaskMode in ATMS.
+                                if (deferred && !task.isAttached()) {
+                                    Slog.w(TAG, "realStartActivity: not locking task " + task
+                                            + ", removed while its lock transition was queued");
+                                    transition.abort();
+                                    return;
+                                }
                                 final ActionChain chain = mService.mChainTracker.start(
                                         "realStartActivity",
                                         transition);
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/LockTaskController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/LockTaskController.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/LockTaskController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/LockTaskController.java
@@ -655,6 +655,13 @@
     void startLockTaskMode(@NonNull Task task, boolean isSystemCaller, int callingUid) {
         if (task.mLockTaskAuth == LOCK_TASK_AUTH_DONT_LOCK) {
             ProtoLog.w(WM_DEBUG_LOCKTASK, "startLockTaskMode: Can't lock due to auth");
             return;
         }
+        // RistOS: never lock a task that is no longer in the hierarchy. A detached Task is
+        // its own root task with no display area; locking it would add a dead task to
+        // mLockTaskModeTasks and NPE in ActivityTaskSupervisor.findTaskToMoveToFront.
+        if (!task.isAttached()) {
+            Slog.w(TAG_LOCKTASK, "startLockTaskMode: task not attached, not locking " + task);
+            return;
+        }
         if (!isSystemCaller) {
             task.mLockTaskUid = callingUid;
             if (task.mLockTaskAuth == LOCK_TASK_AUTH_PINNABLE) {
